WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.297
By the end of this module, I want you to have a practical NumPy toolkit rather than a

00:00:07.297 --> 00:00:10.277
long list of memorized commands.

00:00:10.277 --> 00:00:15.742
You should know several ways to create arrays, including array, arange, linspace, zeros, and ones.

00:00:15.742 --> 00:00:22.312
You should be able to inspect an array using dtype, shape, ndim, and size.

00:00:22.312 --> 00:00:27.907
You should also be comfortable performing calculations without writing unnecessary loops.

00:00:27.907 --> 00:00:33.312
That includes vectorized arithmetic, universal functions, and broadcasting.

00:00:33.312 --> 00:00:35.697
Selection is another major skill.

00:00:35.697 --> 00:00:43.562
You should know how indexing, slicing, Boolean masks, and where let us choose or classify values.

00:00:43.562 --> 00:00:50.757
For analysis, we will use functions such as mean, median, standard deviation, percentiles, minimum,

00:00:50.757 --> 00:00:56.477
and maximum. We will also reshape arrays, combine arrays, generate reproducible random values,

00:00:56.477 --> 00:00:59.242
and work with missing numeric data.

00:00:59.242 --> 00:01:07.237
Most importantly, you should develop the habit of checking an array's shape and data type before assuming that

00:01:07.237 --> 00:01:09.865
a calculation is correct.
